# What NOT to upload. Without this the deploy carries 275 MB of tracked files,
# and @vercel/python bundles the project directory into the function -- against a
# 250 MB unzipped limit. The deploy fails, and the error names the limit rather
# than the four PDFs responsible.
#
# Runtime needs exactly three things from outside travel_planner/ and api/:
# i18n/copy.json, tokens.css, and web/ (built by the static build). Everything
# below is development material.

# 248 MB of hand-made reference itineraries -- read only by
# scripts/check_reference_coverage.py, never at runtime. This one line is most of
# the saving.
data/

# The local SQLite database lives in data/ and is excluded with it, which is
# correct: a serverless function has no durable disk, and api/rpc.py refuses to
# start without TOURIST_DB_URL rather than writing to one.

# Transit feeds, 7.1 GB. Already gitignored, so a Git import never sees them --
# listed anyway because a `vercel deploy` from this directory would.
gtfs/

# Development artefacts.
graphify-out/
artifacts/
tests/
scripts/
supabase/
.venv/
web/node_modules/
# web/dist is NOT excluded: the function serves it. It is gitignored, so it is
# absent at upload and created by the build, and Python functions bundle whatever
# is reachable by then.
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Secrets, belt and braces: both are gitignored, and neither should ever reach a
# build log.
.env
secrets.local.json

# Deployment helpers, not needed by the web function.
deploy/
